    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's getting closer, i like the \"tides of anti-existence\" line. \n\nbut i'm looking at the dashboard and the 'depth' score is still sitting way too low. the producer is being really stickler-ish about this—they mentioned that if the quest dialogue doesn't meet a certain threshold of \"narrative weight\" (basically if that word count metric isn't high enough), the quest might get flagged as \"low effort\" in the build. \n\ni know, i know, i already warned you about the padding. but can you please just really lean into the lore? maybe go into detail about the specific way the Void feels, or the history of the ruins, or just... expand the descriptions? i just need to see that word count move up significantly so it clears the engine's minimums. just make it feel \"heavy\" and \"detailed\" so it doesn't look like we're cutting corners.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
